From 08da1b35fcd5ed923b99ab5b2b0fb11bc3b3c196 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:03:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(app): cross drill stands off the raw stock, not only
 the finished part

Step-1 finding (before this fix): an r10 bar in an r20 raw cylinder,
three stations (+X, +Y, -X). The cross drill measured its standoffs from
the part's facets only: start and feed-entry approach at r15, the
quarter-turn chord's closest approach r15 - 5 mm inside uncut stock.
- mill-turn (A/B/C rotaries stated): generated Ok, verification gate
  empty, POSTED SILENTLY: "G00 X15 Y0 Z10 A0 B90 C0",
  "G00 X21.213 Y0 Z10" -> "G00 X0 Y21.213 Z0" (P0). The verify crate's
  rapid-in-stock law stands down in Mode::Radial, so nothing saw it.
- lathe: blocked, but not for the rapid - "post blocked - 1 warning(s):
  CD1: move 1 cuts past the finish surface" (lathe_axial routes every
  lathe Drill, cross included, through axial_warnings; same with no
  raw stock). With the test bench's default machine both kinds were
  blocked only by the machine-limits clause (no A/B axis stated).

Fix: operation/cross_stock.rs measures the part and the setup's stock
(GenJob::stock_facets, vertex hull: a box's circumscribed radius, a
cylinder's own) about the spindle and stands off the larger; a stock
wider than the part moves each mouth out along its axis to the raw
surface with the floor kept, and its Z top feeds the end-face detour.
Every rapid of the chain is then proven clear of that stock and refused
by name otherwise (which also catches a kernel gap: mouths off their
station's centre line chord inside the bar - now refused). A stock not
reaching past the part, or none, keeps the part-only chain bit for bit.
A cross drill's stamp now digests the setup stock, so re-sizing the bar
stales it. After: start, approach and chord all at r25 (stock r20 +
5 mm standoff); the mill-turn program posts clear.

Fixes #77

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
